      'This guide is for a named operator running a **private** instance. It is not a public-SaaS onboarding manual.\n' +
      '\n' +
      '## Current truth\n' +
      '\n' +
      'Current master: f44d55cad3c24cb49e8793a2cb348387d4c9ce19\n' +
      'Release GO: no\n' +
      '\n' +
      '## First run (local PostgreSQL)\n' +
      '\n' +
      'See [PILOT.md](./PILOT.md) for install, database ports, cookies, and backup. Summary:\n' +
      '\n' +
      '1. Clone the private repository and check out the release-candidate branch.\n' +
      '2. `npm ci` then `sh startup.sh` (or `npm run pg:start` + `npm run dev`).\n' +
      '3. Confirm `npm run check:auth` prints sign-in on.\n' +
      '4. Open the app, create an account, create an organisation.\n' +
      '\n' +
      'Do not create a `.env` file. Local secrets live in gitignored `data/pg-password` and `data/auth-secret` (mode 0600).\n' +
      '\n' +
      '## First organisation\n' +
      '\n' +
      '1. **Create organisation** on the organisations screen.\n' +
      '2. Optional: **Load demonstration pack** (admin/owner). Sample files are labelled demonstration. Nothing is pre-approved. Loading twice is a no-op. A partial load (for example after a rate-limit stop) resumes missing files instead of bricking the pack. The same demonstration filename cannot be stored twice.\n' +
      '3. **Team → Invite**: pick a role (never owner via invite). Copy the bearer code. Share it out of band. Email is a note, not a credential. Codes expire in 7 days; re-invite rotates the code.\n' +
      '4. Joiners sign in separately and paste the code. Matching the invited email is not enough.\n' +
      '\n' +
      'Last owner cannot leave — the Leave button says so and the server refuses. Transfer ownership first, or delete the organisation.\n' +
      '\n' +
      '## Evidence and facts\n' +
      '\n' +
      '- Upload PDF / DOCX / XLSX / TXT (4 MiB). Macros are never executed.\n' +
      '- Heuristic extraction always runs. Optional **Ask model** needs `XAI_API_KEY` and is rate-limited.\n' +
      '- If extraction fails or is stuck on **parsing**, Retry parse. A parse that is still running (under five minutes) is refused. Human corrections to candidates survive retry.\n' +
      '- Reviewers approve or reject candidates. Contributors cannot approve.\n' +
      '- Disagreeing values become CONFLICT. Keep the true value; do not rubber-stamp GREEN.\n' +
      '- Invalidate a source when it is withdrawn. Original bytes remain downloadable. Dependents recompute.\n' +
      '\n' +
      '## Questionnaires and packs\n' +
      '\n' +
      '- Upload a questionnaire from Evidence (check “Treat as questionnaire”) or use the demo PQQ.\n' +
      '- Create a response pack. Status is computed: GREEN / AMBER / RED / EXPIRED / CONFLICT.\n' +
      '- Approving wording does not change evidence status. Exports keep that status.\n' +
      '- Export JSON / XLSX / DOCX. Re-open the file. GREEN rows must cite live facts.\n' +
      '\n' +
      '## Export, leave, delete\n' +
      '\n' +
      '- Admins can download an **organisation snapshot** (metadata, members, facts, answers). File bytes and live invite codes are omitted.\n' +
      '- Any member except the last owner can **leave**.\n' +
      '- Owners can **delete** the organisation by typing its exact name. This wipes memberships, evidence, facts, packs, exports, jobs, and audit.\n' +
      '\n' +
      '## Roles\n' +
      '\n' +
      '| Role | Can |\n' +
      '|---|---|\n' +
      '| viewer | read, download originals |\n' +
      '| contributor | upload, extract, create packs |\n' +
      '| reviewer | approve facts/answers, export, invalidate sources |\n' +
      '| admin | manage members, load demo, snapshot |\n' +
      '| owner | all of the above, including delete organisation |\n' +
      '\n' +
      '## Limits\n' +
      '\n' +
      '- 10 organisations created / user / hour\n' +
      '- 60 uploads / user / hour\n' +
      '- 60 invites / user / org / hour\n' +
      '- 30 AI extracts / user / org / hour\n' +
      '- 25 memberships / user\n' +
      '- 5,000 documents / org (including archived)\n' +
      '- 250 live pending invites / org\n' +
      '- 500 packs / org\n' +
      '- 2,000 stored exports / org\n' +
      '\n' +
      '429 responses say how many seconds to wait.\n' +
      '\n' +
      '## What this product does not do\n' +
      '\n' +
      'No mailer, SAML, OCR, FX conversion, or background worker. Invitations are capability codes shown in the UI. Set `WALLET_SIGNUP_OPEN=false` to reject new email/password **and** new Grok broker OAuth accounts (existing users still sign in). The landing/login/signup UI stays unknown until `/ready` answers 200 with `signupOpen: true`, and fail-closed on a non-OK or failed fetch. Unverified email/password can occupy a mailbox while signup is open (accepted risk K23). There is no password-reset email.\n'
    
  code: 'ERR_ASSERTION'
  name: 'AssertionError'
  expected:
  actual: |-
    # Operator guide
    
    Business Evidence Wallet stores supplier evidence, human-approved facts, questionnaires, cited response packs, and an audit trail. AI may extract or draft. It does not approve facts and cannot turn RED, EXPIRED, or CONFLICT into GREEN.
    
    This guide is for a named operator running a **private** instance. It is not a public-SaaS onboarding manual.
    
    ## Current truth
    
    Current master: f44d55cad3c24cb49e8793a2cb348387d4c9ce19
    Release GO: no
    
    ## First run (local PostgreSQL)
    
    See [PILOT.md](./PILOT.md) for install, database ports, cookies, and backup. Summary:
    
    1. Clone the private repository and check out the release-candidate branch.
    2. `npm ci` then `sh startup.sh` (or `npm run pg:start` + `npm run dev`).
    3. Confirm `npm run check:auth` prints sign-in on.
    4. Open the app, create an account, create an organisation.
    
    Do not create a `.env` file. Local secrets live in gitignored `data/pg-password` and `data/auth-secret` (mode 0600).
    
    ## First organisation
    
    1. **Create organisation** on the organisations screen.
    2. Optional: **Load demonstration pack** (admin/owner). Sample files are labelled demonstration. Nothing is pre-approved. Loading twice is a no-op. A partial load (for example after a rate-limit stop) resumes missing files instead of bricking the pack. The same demonstration filename cannot be stored twice.
    3. **Team → Invite**: pick a role (never owner via invite). Copy the bearer code. Share it out of band. Email is a note, not a credential. Codes expire in 7 days; re-invite rotates the code.
    4. Joiners sign in separately and paste the code. Matching the invited email is not enough.
    
    Last owner cannot leave — the Leave button says so and the server refuses. Transfer ownership first, or delete the organisation.
    
    ## Evidence and facts
    
    - Upload PDF / DOCX / XLSX / TXT (4 MiB). Macros are never executed.
    - Heuristic extraction always runs. Optional **Ask model** needs `XAI_API_KEY` and is rate-limited.
    - If extraction fails or is stuck on **parsing**, Retry parse. A parse that is still running (under five minutes) is refused. Human corrections to candidates survive retry.
    - Reviewers approve or reject candidates. Contributors cannot approve.
    - Disagreeing values become CONFLICT. Keep the true value; do not rubber-stamp GREEN.
    - Invalidate a source when it is withdrawn. Original bytes remain downloadable. Dependents recompute.
    
    ## Questionnaires and packs
    
    - Upload a questionnaire from Evidence (check “Treat as questionnaire”) or use the demo PQQ.
    - Create a response pack. Status is computed: GREEN / AMBER / RED / EXPIRED / CONFLICT.
    - Approving wording does not change evidence status. Exports keep that status.
    - Export JSON / XLSX / DOCX. Re-open the file. GREEN rows must cite live facts.
    
    ## Export, leave, delete
    
    - Admins can download an **organisation snapshot** (metadata, members, facts, answers). File bytes and live invite codes are omitted.
    - Any member except the last owner can **leave**.
    - Owners can **delete** the organisation by typing its exact name. This wipes memberships, evidence, facts, packs, exports, jobs, and audit.
    
    ## Roles
    
    | Role | Can |
    |---|---|
    | viewer | read, download originals |
    | contributor | upload, extract, create packs |
    | reviewer | approve facts/answers, export, invalidate sources |
    | admin | manage members, load demo, snapshot |
    | owner | all of the above, including delete organisation |
    
    ## Limits
    
    - 10 organisations created / user / hour
    - 60 uploads / user / hour
    - 60 invites / user / org / hour
    - 30 AI extracts / user / org / hour
    - 25 memberships / user
    - 5,000 documents / org (including archived)
    - 250 live pending invites / org
    - 500 packs / org
    - 2,000 stored exports / org
    
    429 responses say how many seconds to wait.
    
    ## What this product does not do
    
    No mailer, SAML, OCR, FX conversion, or background worker. Invitations are capability codes shown in the UI. Set `WALLET_SIGNUP_OPEN=false` to reject new email/password **and** new Grok broker OAuth accounts (existing users still sign in). The landing/login/signup UI stays unknown until `/ready` answers 200 with `signupOpen: true`, and fail-closed on a non-OK or failed fetch. Unverified email/password can occupy a mailbox while signup is open (accepted risk K23). There is no password-reset email.
    
